From 7e81a2873e9fb534efea02d1da1408bacf5e38a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:50:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] [lit] Pass FEME_VULKAN_SAFETY_NET_TIMEOUT_MS through to
 tests

lit's default config.environment is a curated whitelist (PATH plus a
handful of sanitizer vars), not a copy of the ambient environment, so a
shell's own FEME_VULKAN_SAFETY_NET_TIMEOUT_MS setting was silently
dropped for every lit-driven run of this suite: FeMe's software ICD got
its five-second default wait-safety-net bound regardless of what the
invoking shell or CMake target had configured, even though the
five-second default is too tight on a host this suite's own parallel
lit workers oversubscribe (a known characteristic, not a hang -- see
Basic/Mandelbrot.test). Add it to the existing with_system_environment
passthrough list alongside the VK_* variables.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Copilot-Session: 1b814ab3-f423-4724-ae98-f676112844de
---
 test/lit.cfg.py | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/test/lit.cfg.py b/test/lit.cfg.py
index 58f68c5..5aadf54 100644
--- a/test/lit.cfg.py
+++ b/test/lit.cfg.py
@@ -59,6 +59,19 @@ llvm_config.with_system_environment(
         "VK_INSTANCE_LAYERS",
         "VK_LOADER_DRIVERS_SELECT",
         "VK_LOADER_DEBUG",
+        # A CPU-based ICD (e.g. FeMe) has no real device latency of its
+        # own to need more than its default wait-safety-net bound, but a
+        # host heavily oversubscribed by this suite's own parallel lit
+        # workers can legitimately push one otherwise-unremarkable large
+        # dispatch's own wait past that default purely from scheduling
+        # contention, not a real hang (see `Basic/Mandelbrot.test`).
+        # Without this passthrough, a shell's own
+        # `FEME_VULKAN_SAFETY_NET_TIMEOUT_MS` setting was silently
+        # dropped here (this suite's own `config.environment` isn't the
+        # full ambient environment), so every lit-driven run of this
+        # suite got the ICD's five-second default regardless of what the
+        # invoking shell or CMake target had configured.
+        "FEME_VULKAN_SAFETY_NET_TIMEOUT_MS",
     ]
 )
 
